# Vigil Plan Mode — Focus Spec (Do Not Implement Until Roadmap Says Go)

**Status:** SPEC / PLANNING ONLY — no code until the user explicitly starts execution.  
**Priority:** Critical product pillar (reordered above IDE LSP in the living roadmap).  
**Related living plan:** `.cursor/rules/00-الخطة-العامة-والأولويات.mdc`  
**Existing related pieces (reuse, don’t reinvent blindly):**
- Runtime checklist today: `manage_plan` + `AgentPlanCard` (during a turn only)
- Product roadmap file is meta for building Vigil — not the in-app Plan Mode

---

> **عربي:** المشكلة اللي بنحلها

## 1. Problem statement

Today Vigil can show a **mid-execution** todo list (`manage_plan`). That is **not** Cursor Plan Mode.

Users need:

1. Discuss a feature / bug / refactor in chat  
2. Agent (or Plan Mode) produces a **structured plan**  
3. User reviews / edits / reorders / removes steps  
4. User explicitly says **Approve / Execute**  
5. Agent executes **step by step** against that approved plan (visible progress, resumable)

Without this, large work is easy to derail, skip steps, or start coding before alignment.

---

> **عربي:** رحلة المستخدم المثالية

## 2. North-star UX (Vigil Plan Mode)

> **عربي:** أوضاع Plan مقابل Agent

### Modes
- [ ] **Chat / Agent mode** — current behavior (can still call `manage_plan` for ad-hoc loops)
- [ ] **Plan mode** — planning-first; default tools are read/search/investigate; **no writes** until Execute
- [ ] Clear mode indicator in chat UI (Plan vs Agent)
- [ ] One-click switch: Plan ↔ Agent (with confirmation if an approved plan is mid-run)

> **عربي:** قسم — Happy path

### Happy path
1. User: describes goal (Arabic or English)  
2. Vigil enters Plan mode (manual toggle **or** auto-suggest when task is large/multi-file)  
3. Vigil gathers just enough context (deep index / `parallel_investigate` / open files / rules)  
4. Vigil outputs a **Plan artifact** (not only markdown prose):
   - Title, goal, assumptions, risks
   - Ordered steps with status, optional file hints, optional acceptance checks
5. User can:
   - Edit step text  
   - Add / delete / reorder steps  
   - Mark a step as optional / blocked  
   - Ask to “revise plan” with feedback without executing  
6. User clicks **Execute plan** (or says موافق نفّذ)  
7. Agent runs with the approved plan as **source of truth**:
   - Exactly one `in_progress`  
   - Updates step status as it goes  
   - Does not silently invent a parallel conflicting checklist unless synced into the same plan  
8. On completion: summary mapped to steps (done / skipped / failed) + files changed + tests run

> **عربي:** الحفظ والاستمرارية

### Persistence
- [ ] Plans are **first-class artifacts** (survive tab reload / app restart)
- [ ] **Primary storage: Firestore** (account-scoped) once Cloud Bridge ships — see `02-جسر-السحابة-الموحد.mdc`
- [ ] Optional local cache / export (VigilDB or `.vigil/plans/`) — **not** the long-term SoR
- [ ] List past plans; reopen; clone; archive
- [ ] Link plan ↔ chat tab / session id

> **عربي:** قواعد زر التنفيذ

### Execute semantics
- [ ] Hard gate: **no write_file / apply_patch / push / PR** while in Plan mode before Execute  
- [ ] After Execute: normal tool policies + Auto-run rules still apply  
- [ ] Pause / Resume / Stop mid-plan  
- [ ] If user interrupts, plan remains with last statuses (not lost)  
- [ ] Failed step: mark `failed`, propose recovery options (retry step / revise plan / continue with remaining)

